        "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
        "revision": 1374278321,
        "heading": "Cultivation",
        "text": "This plant is used for hedging, boundary definition and groundcover in suitably sunny, open locations. Cultivars include 'Strictus' (Irish gorse), a dwarf form, and the double-flowered, non-fruiting 'Flore Pleno', which has gained the Royal Horticultural Society's Award of Garden Merit.",
        "truncated": false
      }
    }
